        <briefdescription>
<para><ref refid="structllvm_1_1coverage_1_1_m_c_d_c_record_1abfea249cd51ba9478b1e85bbc3508418" kindref="member">CondState</ref> represents the evaluation of a condition in an executed test vector, which can be True or False. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>A DontCare is used to mask an unevaluatable condition resulting from short-circuit behavior of logical operators in languages like C/C++. When comparing the evaluation of a condition across executed test vectors, comparisons against a DontCare are effectively ignored. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
